# Transformation A Test: Strip standalone `decide` from `if` conditions

Tests that standalone `if (decide P)` conditions are simplified to `if P`,
while compound boolean conditions with `&&`/`||` retain `decide` wrapping.

## Before Transformation A (Lean4 output):

```
-- Standalone comparison in if:
if (decide (x > 100)) then x + 999 else x + 1

-- Compound boolean in filter lambda (should keep decide):
List.filter (fun (item : Int) => (decide (item > 0)) && (decide (item < 100)))
```

## After Transformation A (Lean4 output):

```
-- Standalone: decide stripped, Prop-based condition
if (x > 100) then x + 999 else x + 1

-- Compound boolean: decide preserved (needed for Bool return type)
List.filter (fun (item : Int) => (decide (item > 0)) && (decide (item < 100)))
```

```catala
declaration scope IfDecideScope:
  input x content integer
  input items content list of integer
  output standalone_if content integer
  output nested_if content integer
  output filtered_items content list of integer

scope IfDecideScope:
  definition standalone_if equals
    if x > 100 then x + 999
    else x + 1

  definition nested_if equals
    if x > 10 then
      if x > 50 then x * 3
      else x * 2
    else x

  definition filtered_items equals
    list of item among items such that item > 0 and item < 100
```
